WEBVTT

00:00:00.162 --> 00:00:03.582
Your career runs on TWO LINES.

00:00:03.332 --> 00:00:06.593
The IQ line. And the EQ line.

00:00:06.343 --> 00:00:09.694
Both keep rising. But one rises FASTER.

00:00:09.714 --> 00:00:13.545
At the very start, IQ does the heavy lifting.

00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:18.421
As a junior, you get a lot of care from the seniors around you.

00:00:18.171 --> 00:00:20.884
Problems land on your desk WELL-DEFINED.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:23.093
The job is to solve them well.

00:00:23.053 --> 00:00:25.173
Then the job changes.

00:00:25.193 --> 00:00:29.013
Scope gets bigger. Problems arrive FUZZY.

00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:32.244
You're working with people from very different backgrounds.

00:00:31.994 --> 00:00:35.274
Hard conflicts. Hard trade-offs.

00:00:35.024 --> 00:00:38.305
And hard conversations — DAILY.

00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:40.235
So IQ still matters.

00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:43.716
EQ just becomes, proportionally, MORE important.

00:00:43.736 --> 00:00:45.275
And it keeps going.

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:47.615
The moment I realised this:

00:00:47.635 --> 00:00:52.145
ONE hard meeting, where everyone walks out actually ALIGNED,

00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:55.188
can save my team WEEKS of work.

00:00:54.938 --> 00:01:00.031
Because alignment moves multiple teams in ONE direction.

00:00:59.781 --> 00:01:05.224
And inside that room, a few sentences can turn the whole meeting.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:06.583
That's ALL EQ playing.

00:01:06.603 --> 00:01:09.223
So here is my working theory:

00:01:09.243 --> 00:01:11.985
The weight keeps shifting.

00:01:11.735 --> 00:01:17.689
The bigger your scope, the more the EQ line carries your career.

00:01:17.664 --> 00:01:20.489
Worth checking your own two lines —

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:21.800
which one have you been TRAINING?
